The separate ‘Cashflow Generation Methodology – Approach Document’ also describes tests of the generated cashflows in Section 7. These include recalculation of baseline principal and interest cashflows outside the cashflow engine and comparison with SS&C outputs. Scenario testing covers 24 selected transactions and 17 historical scenarios. It checks the application of scenario inputs and the plausibility of differences from baseline cashflows. The validator considers these tests relevant to the accuracy of the sampled cashflows.

Section 8 describes ongoing controls and refers to the ‘IRRBB Process Controls and Checklist’ for further details. The documented controls cover product mapping, reconciliation of input data to alternative sources, checks that transferred files match the signed-off inputs, and review of vendor processing logs. They also include checks on the generated cashflows: Treasury and Treasury Risk compare a risk-based sample with cashflows recalculated outside the engine or obtained from alternative sources. Differences are investigated and either resolved or justified. The document requires these controls at least quarterly and before the cashflows are used for risk estimation. These upstream controls complement the import and processing checks within the CSRBB model.

Where a cashflow exception is confirmed, it is handled through the escalation process described in chapter 3.6 of the DOI, under which all controls are signed off, and any data exception is escalated. The validator reviewed this process and considers it adequate.
